---
// Planning — how you actually get a drive. Replaces the old "Two ways to ride"
// (Modes.astro) section, whose second way was FREE ROAM: deleted outright in 1.1
// (docs/designs/drives-first-1-1.md, D1). That section's own header argued roam was
// "real shipped product (the route player + RoamEngine)" — RoamEngine was deleted in
// 3944e5f, so the justification outlived the thing it justified.
//
// ⚠ This section is now the ONLY place the front door says the planning is a
// CONVERSATION, which is the single biggest product change in 1.1 and the thing that
// makes Skipper not-a-catalog. Card 1's art deliberately mirrors the app's own
// TurnBubble language (rider = right-aligned sunken bubble; skipper = full-width prose
// behind a 2pt pine speaker rule) so the page looks like the product.
//
// ⚠ The closing line is a claim about CODE, not a flourish: the planner emits curated
// anchor IDS and the server re-asserts endpoint_eligible at the wire before any billed
// Routes call (INV-1). An off-list ask gets an in-persona "don't know that one" — never
// a geocode. If that ever stops being true, this paragraph is part of the change.
import { CAR_BODY_PATH } from '../carBody'
---

<section class="section planning" id="planning">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="planning__head">
      <span class="kicker">Planning</span>
      <h2 class="title">Just tell him where you’re going.</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="planning__grid">
      <!-- You talk -->
      <article class="plan-card framed">
        <div class="plan-card__badge"><span class="badge badge--pine badge--dot">You talk</span></div>
        <svg class="plan-card__art" viewBox="0 0 260 130" aria-hidden="true">
          <!-- the rider's line: right-aligned, sunken — the app's rider bubble -->
          <rect x="94" y="16" width="148" height="36" rx="10"
            fill="var(--surface-sunken)" stroke="var(--keyline)" stroke-width="1.4"></rect>
          <g fill="var(--ink-faint)">
            <rect x="108" y="28" width="104" height="4" rx="2"></rect>
            <rect x="108" y="38" width="70" height="4" rx="2"></rect>
          </g>
          <!-- the skipper's reply: prose behind a pine speaker rule -->
          <rect x="18" y="68" width="3" height="46" rx="1.5" fill="var(--accent)"></rect>
          <g fill="var(--ink-faint)">
            <rect x="32" y="72" width="178" height="4" rx="2"></rect>
            <rect x="32" y="85" width="206" height="4" rx="2"></rect>
            <rect x="32" y="98" width="138" height="4" rx="2"></rect>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <p class="plan-card__body">
          “We’re heading from Tahoe City down to Emerald Bay, and we’ve got about two hours.” That’s it —
          that’s the whole interface. No menus, no dragging pins, no picking stops off a list.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- He plans it -->
      <article class="plan-card framed">
        <div class="plan-card__badge"><span class="badge badge--teal badge--dot">He plans it</span></div>
        <svg class="plan-card__art" viewBox="0 0 260 130" aria-hidden="true">
          <ellipse cx="130" cy="65" rx="98" ry="44" fill="none" stroke="var(--track-inactive)"
            stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="4 4"></ellipse>
          <!-- ordered stop pips -->
          <g fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.6">
            <circle cx="130" cy="21" r="6"></circle>
            <circle cx="228" cy="65" r="6"></circle>
            <circle cx="130" cy="109" r="6"></circle>
            <circle cx="32" cy="65" r="6"></circle>
          </g>
          <g fill="var(--accent)" font-family="'Overpass Mono', monospace" font-size="7.5" text-anchor="middle">
            <text x="130" y="23.6">1</text>
            <text x="228" y="67.6">2</text>
            <text x="130" y="111.6">3</text>
            <text x="32" y="67.6">4</text>
          </g>
          <!-- car token mid-route -->
          <g transform="translate(176 96) scale(0.82)" style="color:var(--amber)">
            <path d={CAR_BODY_PATH} fill="currentColor"></path>
            <circle cx="10.5" cy="14.4" r="2.8" fill="var(--surface-raised)"></circle>
            <circle cx="25" cy="14.4" r="2.8" fill="var(--surface-raised)"></circle>
          </g>
        </svg>
        <p class="plan-card__body">
          He knows which places are worth slowing down for, and he lays them out along your route in the
          order you’ll actually meet them. Download it and go — then he does the talking.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <p class="planning__foot body-dim">
      He’ll only ever send you somewhere real. The Skipper works from a list of places we curated by
      hand — he can’t invent a destination, and he won’t try. Ask him for one that isn’t on it and he’ll
      tell you so, in his own words.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .planning__head {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }
  .planning__head .kicker {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }
  .planning__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xl);
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .planning__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-2xl);
    }
  }
  .plan-card {
    background: var(--surface-raised);
    padding: var(--space-2xl);
  }
  .plan-card__badge {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .plan-card__art {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    background: var(--surface-sunken);
    border: var(--border-thin) solid var(--keyline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-md);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .plan-card__body {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
  }
  .planning__foot {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
</style>
